  "target_says_no_aki_there": {
   "icd_label": 0.6303,
   "kdigo_label": 0.0464
  },
  "coincidence_of_kdigo_target_and_constraint": 0.9536,
  "violation_drop_implied_by_target_base_rates": 0.584,
  "violation_drop_observed": 0.7184,
  "observed_over_implied": 1.23,
  "share_attributable_to_base_rate": 0.813,
  "reading": "On the constraint-applicable subgroup the KDIGO target is already positive for 95.4% of cases against 37.0% for the ICD target, so a model fitted to it starts near-compliant by construction. Base rates alone imply a violation-rate drop of 0.584; the observed drop is 0.718. Roughly 81% of the effect is therefore target arithmetic and the remainder is learned. This is a valid POSITIVE CONTROL -- it shows the constraint is triggerable and the harness responds -- but it is NOT clean causal evidence that a guideline-faithful target fixes compliance, and it should not be promoted to the paper's primary causal claim."
 },
